\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Takeaway: one explanation, three predictions, three confirmations, and a scope boundary the same explanation predicts.} The explanation is that a reference on a multi-valid task is one sample from the valid set and the judge anchors on it. Anchoring is in points of the judge's 0--10 scale; inflation and the training wedge are in baseline standard deviations of the judge's own score distribution. Intervals, caveats, and the predictions that failed are in the sections named.}}{2}{table.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
